Market Challenges
Integrating sensor measurements into utility control-room systems requires reliable communications, calibration, cybersecurity and operational validation. Installation on energized lines also involves specialised equipment, safety procedures and engineering approvals.

Market Restraints
Sensorless weather-based rating models can provide an alternative to physical instrumentation, particularly on less constrained transmission corridors. High installation and maintenance costs, long validation cycles and physical bottlenecks elsewhere in the network can also limit sensor deployment.

